From: Banks Troutman <banks.troutman@oxos.com>
Subject: [PATCH] video: tegra: dc: allow portrait resolutions above 2160p

The HDMI mode filter rejects any mode with yres > 2160, which blocks
portrait displays like the Waveshare WS-55-2K (1440x2560@50Hz). The
display controller hardware supports up to 4096x4096, so raise the
vertical limit to match the horizontal one.

Signed-off-by: Banks Troutman <banks.troutman@oxos.com>
---
 nvidia/drivers/video/tegra/dc/hdmi2.0.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/nvidia/drivers/video/tegra/dc/hdmi2.0.c b/nvidia/drivers/video/tegra/dc/hdmi2.0.c
index abcdef1..1234567 100644
--- a/nvidia/drivers/video/tegra/dc/hdmi2.0.c
+++ b/nvidia/drivers/video/tegra/dc/hdmi2.0.c
@@ -336,7 +336,7 @@ static bool tegra_hdmi_fb_mode_filter(const struct tegra_dc *dc,
 	if (!mode->pixclock)
 		return false;

-	if (mode->xres > 4096 || mode->yres > 2160)
+	if (mode->xres > 4096 || mode->yres > 4096)
 		return false;

 #if defined(CONFIG_TEGRA_YUV_BYPASS_MODE_FILTER)
